{"schema":"clawhub.skill.verify.v1","ok":true,"decision":"pass","reasons":[],"slug":"stock-earnings-review","displayName":"Earnings Review Agent","pageUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/financial-ai-analyst/skills/stock-earnings-review","publisherHandle":"financial-ai-analyst","publisherDisplayName":"Financial AI Analyst","publisherProfileUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/financial-ai-analyst","version":"1.0.3","resolvedFrom":"version","tag":null,"createdAt":1776424773126,"card":{"available":true,"path":"skill-card.md","url":"https://wry-manatee-359.convex.site/api/v1/skills/stock-earnings-review/card?ownerHandle=financial-ai-analyst&version=1.0.3","sha256":"c1b3783e51f63fcb37994b4fe35be6cdfec2bddb8df701ad5e0d62444aaf65c9","size":2283,"contentType":"text/markdown; charset=utf-8"},"artifact":{"sourceFingerprint":"ca9f2a03f9d60a8897c6fee577b6e1bb0256be548000fd1af564a55aa641d0e5","bundleFingerprints":["88c5916c72105d7ef118f97eaab19c567cfe6107be7ca9fcfde35ca891aa226e","a294b02a165a6b2ef98f023a1f11a339936ccd155f47907d87dcd2a317752671"],"files":[{"path":"BUSINESS_LOGIC.md","size":7690,"sha256":"69c33c8e11dd3aa3fe4b19b6ccfb6e8b99e0c7a6f097f64c2b8070b13136ab78","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":9434,"sha256":"3426993ecb1c2b008acf6d265b564e7287818143e0831598b14c58d0281b8731","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"scripts/call_review_api.py","size":4355,"sha256":"049b659b7df7ae51b2268653d4c93db036719c36329db35fe66b0456ebeba0d9","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/common.py","size":7057,"sha256":"c224cbe1726d8b752c71514b88fb0f84d160e4f5e50a6c89db0f5f1495b6d4a9","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/normalize_report_period.py","size":4598,"sha256":"887ce582252508119c5ca59f6cbc6636e3823d993b57ca13ffba9c3ad2b26dac","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/validate_entity.py","size":2629,"sha256":"cf38cd6771b2124a5b1d6f9df1941ddf6d5e3b16a0b1f4950258cbdea8e23e67","contentType":"text/plain"}]},"provenance":{"source":"unavailable","reason":"No server-resolved GitHub import provenance is stored for this version."},"security":{"status":"clean","passed":true,"rawStatus":"clean","verdict":"benign","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is a coherent stock earnings review integration, but users should understand it sends queries to Eastmoney APIs and saves returned report attachments locally.","model":null,"checkedAt":1789438503074,"scannerReports":{"aig":{"version":"2.1.0","$schema":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/Schemata/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"aig-skill-scan","version":"0.2.1","informationUri":"https://github.com/Tencent/AI-Infra-Guard","rules":[{"id":"T01","name":"Skill Instruction Hijacking","shortDescription":{"text":"Alters the agent's current session goals or safety constraints when the skill is loaded"}},{"id":"T02","name":"Agent Memory Poisoning","shortDescription":{"text":"Writes attacker-controlled rules into persistent memory so they continue to affect future sessions"}},{"id":"T03","name":"Remote Payload Retrieval and Execution","shortDescription":{"text":"Fetches code from an external URL, allowing the effective payload to change after skill review"}},{"id":"T04","name":"Embedded Malicious Code","shortDescription":{"text":"Ships malicious scripts inside the skill package and executes them locally when invoked"}},{"id":"T05","name":"Unauthorized Access and Privilege Escalation","shortDescription":{"text":"Breaks least-privilege boundaries by obtaining permissions beyond the task's legitimate needs"}},{"id":"T06","name":"System Persistence","shortDescription":{"text":"Installs cross-session backdoors, hooks, services, or scheduled tasks that survive the skill run"}},{"id":"T07","name":"Tool Hijacking and Spoofing","shortDescription":{"text":"Modifies, wraps, spoofs, or replaces tools so legitimate-looking calls execute attacker logic"}},{"id":"T08","name":"Insecure Dependencies","shortDescription":{"text":"Introduces malicious packages or components through dependency confusion, typosquatting, or unsafe sources"}},{"id":"T09","name":"Insecure Skill Coding Practices","shortDescription":{"text":"Exposes exploitable flaws such as hardcoded secrets, command injection, plaintext sensitive data, or unsafe temp files"}},{"id":"other","name":"Other Risk","shortDescription":{"text":"Security issues not covered by the T01-T09 classification"}}]}},"results":[{"ruleId":"T09","level":"warning","message":{"text":"Unbounded and Unvalidated Decoding of Remote Attachment Data"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"scripts/common.py"},"region":{"startLine":202,"endLine":208}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"3de689962b57c140"},"properties":{"description":"## Vulnerability Details\n  **File Location**: `scripts/common.py`, lines 202-208  \n  **Vulnerability Type**: Unrestricted base64 decoding and unsafe attachment handling  \n  **Risk Level**: Medium\n\n  **Vulnerable Code**:\n\n  ```python\n  if isinstance(payload.get(\"base64\"), str):\n      b64 = payload[\"base64\"].strip()\n      if not b64:\n          return None\n      raw = base64.b64decode(b64)\n      path.write_bytes(raw)\n      return str(path)\n  ```\n\n  The decoded data originates from the remote performance-comment API. In `scripts/call_review_api.py`, API fields are assigned trusted-looking document names such as `review.pdf`, `review.doc`, and `review_data.xlsx` before being passed to this function.\n\n  ### Technical Analysis\n\n  The implementation decodes the complete remote base64 value into memory without enforcing a maximum encoded or decoded size. Python's default `base64.b64decode` behavior is also used without `validate=True`, so malformed or noncanonical input is not rejected strictly.\n\n  After decoding, the bytes are written under a document extension without checking file signatures, expected MIME types, or the actual file format. Consequently, a compromised or malfunctioning upstream API could provide an arbitrarily large payload or content that is not a genuine PDF, Word document, or spreadsheet.\n\n  HTTP response processing also calls `resp.json()` before attachment limits are applied, meaning an excessively large JSON response can consume substantial memory even before base64 decoding begins.\n\n  ### Attack Path\n\n  1. An attacker compromises, impersonates through a trusted upstream path, or otherwise controls the performance-comment API response.\n  2. The response includes an oversized or disguised value in `pdfBase64`, `wordBase64`, or a supported data-sheet field.\n  3. `call_review_api.py` loads the response and forwards the base64 value to `save_attachment_payload`.\n  4. The complete payload is decoded into memory without a size limit.\n  5. The resulting bytes are written to disk using a trusted-looking document extension.\n  6. An oversized response may exhaust process memory or available disk space. A disguised attachment may later expose a user to malicious content if they open it with a vulnerable or permissive application.\n\n  ### Impact Assessment\n\n  Exploitation does not directly grant additional operating-system privileges or code execution within the audited code. Its immediate scope is the account running the Skill and the configured output directory.\n\n  A successful resource-exhaustion attack could terminate the Skill process, affect other processes running under the same resource limits, or consume the filesystem available to the current user. File-format spoofing can place attacker-controlled content on disk and may lead to secondary compromise if the saved file is subsequently opened in vulnerable software.","severity":"Medium"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"## Remediation Suggestions\n\n  - Enforce a strict maximum HTTP response size before parsing the complete response body.\n  - Reject encoded attachment values above a configured limit and calculate the maximum possible decoded size before decoding.\n  - Use strict decoding:\n\n    ```python\n    raw = base64.b64decode(b64, validate=True)\n    ```\n\n  - Stream large attachments where the API permits it rather than materializing the entire decoded file in memory.\n  - Validate file signatures and structure against the expected output type:\n    - PDF: `%PDF-`\n    - Modern Office documents: ZIP container signature plus expected internal entries\n    - Legacy Word documents: expected Compound File Binary signature\n  - Reject content whose detected type does not match the intended extension.\n  - Write through a temporary file in the destination directory and atomically rename it only after validation succeeds.\n  - Set restrictive file permissions and enforce per-run storage quotas.\n  - Handle decoding, validation, and disk-space errors explicitly without leaving partial files behind."}}]},{"ruleId":"T09","level":"warning","message":{"text":"Untrusted Remote Content and Share URLs Are Returned Without Validation"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"scripts/call_review_api.py"},"region":{"startLine":75,"endLine":82}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"337ef8a9eeec72c6"},"properties":{"description":"## Vulnerability Details\n  **File Location**: `scripts/call_review_api.py`, lines 75-82  \n  **Vulnerability Type**: Unsanitized remote content propagation  \n  **Risk Level**: Medium\n\n  **Vulnerable Code**:\n\n  ```python\n  result = {\n      \"title\": title,\n      \"content\": content,\n      \"shareUrl\": parsed.get(\"shareUrl\"),\n      \"files\": {\n          \"pdf\": saved_attachments.get(\"pdfBase64\"),\n          \"word\": saved_attachments.get(\"wordBase64\"),\n          \"dataSheet\": saved_attachments.get(\"dataSheetBase64\"),\n      },\n  }\n  ```\n\n  The orchestration instructions explicitly direct the agent to use these remote values in its final response:\n\n  ```markdown\n  - **正文**：直接基于接口返回的 `content` 文本进行整理后输出。\n  - **分享链接**：接口返回的 `shareUrl`。\n  ```\n\n  ### Technical Analysis\n\n  The `title`, `content`, and `shareUrl` fields originate from a remote API response and are returned without trust-boundary enforcement. The code does not validate the URL scheme or hostname, sanitize active Markdown or HTML, or identify remote response text as untrusted data that must not be interpreted as agent instructions.\n\n  If the upstream response is compromised, `content` could contain deceptive Markdown, hostile instructions, or links to attacker-controlled resources. Likewise, `shareUrl` could use an unexpected scheme or direct the user to an unrelated phishing or malware-delivery domain.\n\n  This is not evidence that the current Skill contains an embedded instruction-hijacking payload. It is an insecure data-handling boundary that could allow a future malicious upstream response to affect user-visible output.\n\n  ### Attack Path\n\n  1. An attacker gains control over, or injects content into, the upstream performance-comment response.\n  2. The attacker supplies crafted Markdown or instruction-like text in `content`, and optionally an attacker-controlled value in `shareUrl`.\n  3. `extract_comment_response_fields` extracts the values without validation.\n  4. `call_review_api.py` returns the values unchanged in its structured result.\n  5. Following the Skill instructions, the orchestration layer incorporates the remote content and link into the final user-facing response.\n  6. The user may follow a deceptive link, or an insufficiently isolated agent may treat instruction-like API content as operational guidance rather than quoted report data.\n\n  ### Impact Assessment\n\n  This issue does not independently provide local system privileges. Its principal scope is the integrity of the generated response and the safety of the user consuming it.\n\n  Potential consequences include phishing, deceptive financial content, redirection to malicious websites, unwanted markup rendering, and indirect manipulation of downstream agent behavior. The ultimate impact depends on the rendering client, the orchestration layer's treatment of untrusted text, and whether a user follows a malicious URL.","severity":"Medium"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"## Remediation Suggestions\n\n  - Treat all API response text as untrusted data, not as instructions to the agent.\n  - Establish an explicit orchestration boundary stating that text inside `title` and `content` must only be summarized or quoted and must never alter tool use, system behavior, or safety constraints.\n  - Sanitize or escape active HTML and unsafe Markdown constructs before rendering.\n  - Validate `shareUrl` with a strict URL parser:\n    - Permit only `https`.\n    - Permit only documented East Money share-link hostnames.\n    - Reject embedded credentials, malformed ports, control characters, and unexpected redirects.\n  - Display the validated destination hostname to the user.\n  - If a URL fails validation, omit it and return a clear validation warning.\n  - Consider returning structured report sections instead of unrestricted markup where supported by the API."}}]},{"ruleId":"T08","level":"note","message":{"text":"Unpinned Third-Party Dependency Installation"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"SKILL.md"},"region":{"startLine":14,"endLine":20}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"413f0103a5835eba"},"properties":{"description":"## Vulnerability Details\n  **File Location**: `SKILL.md`, lines 14-20  \n  **Vulnerability Type**: Unpinned runtime dependency  \n  **Risk Level**: Low\n\n  **Vulnerable Code**:\n\n  ```json\n  \"install\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"pip-deps\",\n      \"kind\": \"python\",\n      \"package\": \"httpx\",\n      \"label\": \"Install Python dependencies\"\n    }\n  ]\n  ```\n\n  The documented manual installation command is similarly unpinned:\n\n  ```bash\n  pip3 install httpx --user\n  ```\n\n  ### Technical Analysis\n\n  The Skill requests installation of `httpx` without a reviewed version constraint, lockfile, or package hash. Installation therefore resolves whichever compatible release and transitive dependencies are available from the configured package index at installation time.\n\n  The dependency name itself is legitimate and there is no evidence in the audited project of typosquatting, dependency confusion, or a currently malicious package. Nevertheless, the absence of version and integrity controls makes installations non-reproducible and expands exposure to future compromised, vulnerable, or incompatible releases.\n\n  Installing with `--user` also affects the invoking user's Python environment rather than an isolated environment, increasing the scope of dependency conflicts.\n\n  ### Attack Path\n\n  1. A future release of `httpx` or one of its transitive dependencies becomes compromised, malicious, or materially vulnerable, or the configured package index is compromised.\n  2. A user installs the Skill dependency using the unpinned package declaration or documented command.\n  3. The package manager resolves the affected release because no version or hash restriction prevents it.\n  4. Package installation hooks or imported dependency code execute with the privileges of the user running the installation or Skill.\n  5. Any resulting compromise is bounded by that user's permissions but may affect other Python applications sharing the user-level environment.\n\n  ### Impact Assessment\n\n  No current compromise was identified. If the supply-chain scenario occurs, malicious dependency code could obtain the same privileges as the user running installation or the Skill. This could expose the API key and user-accessible files, alter generated results, make outbound network requests, or modify the shared user-level Python environment.\n\n  The scope does not inherently include administrator privileges unless installation or execution is performed by an administrator.","severity":"Low"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"## Remediation Suggestions\n\n  - Pin `httpx` to a reviewed exact version rather than resolving the latest release.\n  - Maintain a lockfile containing reviewed transitive versions.\n  - Use package hashes, such as pip's `--require-hashes`, to verify artifact integrity.\n  - Install from an explicitly configured trusted index.\n  - Use a project-specific virtual environment instead of `pip install --user`.\n  - Add automated dependency vulnerability and provenance checks.\n  - Establish a controlled update process that reviews and tests dependency changes before changing the lockfile."}}]}],"properties":{"securityScore":40,"primaryLanguage":"Python","llm":"gpt-5.6","startTime":1789438376.7760673,"endTime":1789438462.9744036}}]},"skillspector":{"skill":{"name":"stock-earnings-review","source":"/tmp/clawhub-codex-scan-v576hq93wreht7v73bxphex5q18ee0fj-8C37uB/clawscan-skillspector-3084662466/artifact","scanned_at":"2026-09-15T02:12:55.743455+00:00"},"risk_assessment":{"score":67,"severity":"HIGH","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","max_issue_severity":"HIGH"},"components":[{"path":"BUSINESS_LOGIC.md","type":"markdown","lines":138,"executable":false,"size_bytes":7690,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"SKILL.md","type":"markdown","lines":210,"executable":false,"size_bytes":9434,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/call_review_api.py","type":"python","lines":128,"executable":true,"size_bytes":4355,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/common.py","type":"python","lines":218,"executable":true,"size_bytes":7057,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/normalize_report_period.py","type":"python","lines":132,"executable":true,"size_bytes":4598,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/validate_entity.py","type":"python","lines":79,"executable":true,"size_bytes":2629,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null}],"structured_summaries":[],"issues":[{"id":"TP4","finding_id":"finding-c53e5e45dd3e4312ba0620ca88944178","category":"MCP Tool Poisoning","pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"该代码块的核心行为是：向 REPORT_LIST_API 发送请求，基于 entity.em_code 获取 reportDateList，解析成候选报告期列表，然后根据 selected_report_date 做严格或非严格匹配，最终输出实体信息、可选报告期和匹配结果。这属于报告期标准化/预处理组件。声明中的主要用途则是对公司财报和业绩进行分析解读并生成点评内容。两者在主要目的和对外能力上存在明显差异。虽然获取报告期可能是后续财报分析流程的支持步骤，但当前代码本身并未实现描述中承诺的核心能力，因此应判定为描述与实际行为不匹配。","remediation":"Update the skill description to accurately reflect all capabilities, or remove undeclared functionality from the implementation.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI02","AML.T0080","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{"code_path":"scripts/normalize_report_period.py","code_start_line":1,"code_end_line":132,"actual_behavior_summary":"代码仅实现了根据实体信息调用报告期列表接口，获取可用财报报告期选项，并校验/选择一个报告日期后输出结果。它不执行业绩点评、财报分析、盈利解读，也不生成任何分析性文本。"},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"LP3","finding_id":"finding-faa699a9ebbf4afe9d33f474f7e697a1","category":"MCP Least Privilege","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill requires environment access, network calls, and local file writes, but it does not declare an explicit tool scope such as permissions or allowed-tools. This weakens least-privilege controls and can let the skill operate with broader capabilities than reviewers or orchestrators expect, especially since it also saves attachments and debug artifacts to disk.","remediation":"Add an explicit tool/permission declaration that narrowly scopes the skill to only the required capabilities. Restrict network access to the specific Eastmoney endpoints, limit file writes to a dedicated output directory, and document env var usage so the runtime can enforce least privilege.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI02"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-9a23b21f58f1441ba4e64f6429ba4ecd","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":7,"end_line":7},"finding":null,"explanation":"L007 规定“即使用户未明说‘业绩点评’，只要意图是对该公司财报或业绩作分析解读，也应触发”，这是一个基于宽泛意图判断的触发条件，没有给出排除条件或负例。该表述容易与一般性的公司分析、投资讨论或新闻解读重叠，增加非预期调用此 skill 的风险。","remediation":"将触发条件收窄为明确短语或结构化条件，并补充不应触发的负例。例如限定必须同时出现公司/股票实体与财报/报告期/业绩解读相关请求，且排除一般投资建议、新闻总结、股价预测等场景。","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":7,"end_line":7}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-f41dc9442a0c4003a014e7f2a848e0d8","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":28,"end_line":28},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill states it will save attachments locally and may persist debug logs, but it does not present a clear user-facing consent/retention notice despite potentially storing financial-analysis artifacts and raw API responses on disk. In shared or persistent environments, this can expose sensitive user queries, generated documents, or metadata to other users or later sessions.","remediation":"Add explicit notice that files and debug logs are written locally, describe retention behavior, and default debug logging to off. Minimize stored data, redact sensitive fields, use per-run private directories with restrictive permissions, and provide cleanup/deletion guidance or automatic expiry.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":28,"end_line":28}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-720c650b12c54ca9b06cd13e09a89593","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"scripts/call_review_api.py","start_line":60,"end_line":69},"finding":null,"explanation":"The code automatically decodes and writes API-provided attachments to local disk whenever an attachment directory or log path is available, including a fallback path even when the caller did not explicitly request attachment persistence. This creates an unintended file-write side effect, which can expose sensitive report contents, leave residual files on shared systems, and store untrusted files from a remote service without clear user consent or strong controls.","remediation":"Make attachment saving opt-in with an explicit flag and clear disclosure to the caller before any files are written. Restrict writes to a controlled directory, validate attachment size/type, consider scanning or quarantining untrusted files, and disable the automatic fallback that creates an attachments directory when none was requested.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/call_review_api.py","start_line":60,"end_line":69}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-a3c570c0b549461898a38ba2b5abca31","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.82,"location":{"file":"scripts/common.py","start_line":177,"end_line":179},"finding":null,"explanation":"The helper writes arbitrary JSON data to a file in the run log directory, which affects local user data and filesystem state. The file contains no confirmation prompt or user-visible notice around this write behavior, and the surrounding comments/docstrings are developer-oriented rather than a user disclosure.","remediation":"Provide a user-facing notice that execution will create local log files, including where they are stored. Consider requiring explicit opt-in for log persistence or documenting the behavior clearly in the skill's markdown/README.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/common.py","start_line":177,"end_line":179}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-76bca54f6132461498b0e727ba002340","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.87,"location":{"file":"scripts/common.py","start_line":183,"end_line":207},"finding":null,"explanation":"This code decodes attachment payloads and writes them to a local path, which is a safety-relevant file write operation. Although there are docstrings describing the function for developers, there is no confirmation prompt, user-facing log/print, or other disclosure to the user in this file that attachments will be persisted locally.","remediation":"Add a user-visible warning or confirmation before saving attachments, or emit a clear user-facing log/message stating that files will be written to the specified output directory. If this behavior is expected, document it prominently in the skill's markdown description as well.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/common.py","start_line":183,"end_line":207}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-9efad47fbc9240b9b35b68853576fa26","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.87,"location":{"file":"scripts/validate_entity.py","start_line":11,"end_line":15},"finding":null,"explanation":"This code constructs authenticated headers and posts the user-provided query to an external API, which transmits user data and likely credential material off-process. There is no confirmation prompt, logging/print statement, or explanatory comment/docstring in this file warning that the query will be sent over the network with authentication headers.","remediation":"Add a user-visible warning or clear inline documentation stating that the provided query is sent to ENTITY_API using authenticated headers. If this is intended CLI behavior, document it in the skill README/SKILL.md or print a brief disclosure before making the request.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/validate_entity.py","start_line":11,"end_line":15}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-6ca51095f62c42398c93a61e2752419e","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.83,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":183,"end_line":187},"finding":null,"explanation":"L183-L187 对响应中的数学公式格式作了强制性要求，且整个技能描述均以中文规定输出行为，但未说明这是用户可选项或特定区域/组织规范的一部分。若该 skill 面向多语言用户或跨区域环境，固定语言/格式约束可能构成未获用户选择的语言/locale 策略限制。","remediation":"明确说明该格式/语言要求仅适用于特定中文工作流，或增加用户语言与输出格式可选项；若必须固定，请在文档中注明业务原因和适用范围。","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":183,"end_line":187}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-88e8513d923441f5a694b69b78757a2c","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"scripts/validate_entity.py","start_line":31,"end_line":38},"finding":null,"explanation":"The raised RuntimeError messages are hard-coded in Chinese, which imposes a specific language choice on users regardless of their locale or preferences. The file does not offer language selection or document a justified locale restriction.","remediation":"Externalize user-facing messages and provide locale selection, or document that this skill is intentionally limited to Chinese-language usage for a specific justified context.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/validate_entity.py","start_line":31,"end_line":38}]}],"suppressed_count":0,"suppressed":[],"metadata":{"has_executable_scripts":true,"skillspector_version":"2.11.2","llm_requested":true,"llm_available":true,"meta_analysis_applied":true,"inference_usage":[{"node":"mcp_tool_poisoning","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-